# TC-105 seed-and-wire verification

> Date: 2026-05-13
> Branch: `ralph/tc-105-seed-and-wire-up`
> Companion to: `docs/1.1.0-upgrade-evidence/tc105-fast-query-diagnosis.log` (PR #62)
> Test: `tests/e2e/test_02_chat.py::test_tc105_query_results_table`

## What changed

After PR #62 unblocked the Manager → MCP wiring, the fast-query path
reaches NebulaGraph but returned 0 rows because the `honeybadge` space
had no PurchaseOrder data. The repo already shipped a complete seed
script (`deploy/docker/nebula_seed.py`) — it just wasn't wired into the
bootstrap. This branch:

1. Adds `deploy/docker/seed-nebula.sh` — a docker-based wrapper around
   the existing Python seed script. Pulls `python:3.11-slim`, mounts the
   seed script, installs `nebula3-python` from the Aliyun mirror, and
   runs against the `honeybadge-nebula-graphd` container on the
   `honeybadge-network`. No host Python or pip required.
2. Calls it from `scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh --setup-only` right after
   `init-nebula.sh` (schema) and before `init-workers.sh` (Manager + MCP
   wiring).

The seed script itself is idempotent (`INSERT VERTEX/EDGE IF NOT
EXISTS`), so re-running is safe.

