## End-to-end verification

```
$ docker exec honeybadge-hiclaw-manager bash -c '
    bash /opt/honeybadge/config/manager/agent/skills/fast-query/fast-query.sh \
      --question "查询前5个采购订单" --user-id admin --task-id tc105-seeded'
{
  "success": true,
  "columns": [
    "po.PurchaseOrder.po_number",
    "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date",
    "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount",
    "po.PurchaseOrder.status"
  ],
  "rows": [
    {"po.PurchaseOrder.po_number": "PO100000102", "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date": 1730505600, "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount": 765306, "po.PurchaseOrder.status": "APPROVED"},
    {"po.PurchaseOrder.po_number": "PO100000181", "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date": 1720742400, "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount": 368543, "po.PurchaseOrder.status": "APPROVED"},
    {"po.PurchaseOrder.po_number": "PO100000266", "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date": 1712534400, "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount":  13798, "po.PurchaseOrder.status": "APPROVED"},
    {"po.PurchaseOrder.po_number": "PO100000273", "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date": 1714348800, "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount":  62819, "po.PurchaseOrder.status": "APPROVED"},
    {"po.PurchaseOrder.po_number": "PO100100204", "po.PurchaseOrder.order_date": 1726704000, "po.PurchaseOrder.total_amount": 530612, "po.PurchaseOrder.status": "APPROVED"}
  ],
  "row_count": 5,
  "execution_time_ms": 51,
  "trace_id": "TRC-20260514-004642-61c23c51",
  "warnings": []
}
EXIT=0
```

This payload is exactly the shape `forward-to-user.sh --result-json`
turns into x-honeybadge contract 002, which `useMatrixChat.ts` parses
into `message.message_type = 'query_result'` + `metadata.raw_data` +
`metadata.columns`. The frontend's render gate
(`ChatMessage.vue:26-39`) requires `metadata?.raw_data?.length > 0` —
satisfied here.

## What pytest run is pending

Full Playwright run (`pytest -c pytest.ini tests/e2e/test_02_chat.py`)
was not executed on this Windows host: Python 3.14 + asyncio +
Playwright + `pytest-timeout` deadlock per the pre-existing TC-110
limitation (see `docs/1.1.0-upgrade-followups.md`). The pipeline is
healthy at the data-shape level; the remaining work is a CI/Linux
verification run.

To run on a Linux box / ECS:

```
./scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh --filter chat
# (which now seeds Nebula automatically as part of --setup-only)
```

or just the single test:

```
pytest -c pytest.ini \
  tests/e2e/test_02_chat.py::TestQueryResults::test_tc105_query_results_table \
  --timeout=200 -v
```
